WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.420
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.129
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:14.613
Unit twenty-one: Street Food. In this unit, you will describe the taste of food.

4
00:00:15.617 --> 00:00:16.664
Street food.

5
00:00:17.364 --> 00:00:21.163
Street food means food sold outside from small stalls or carts.

6
00:00:21.463 --> 00:00:23.544
Phnom Penh has amazing street food.

7
00:00:24.244 --> 00:00:26.804
Your turn. Say: Street food.

8
00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:30.539
Street food.

9
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:32.342
Stall.

10
00:00:33.042 --> 00:00:36.319
Stall means a small table or shop in the street or a market.

11
00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:38.874
The noodle stall is always busy.

12
00:00:39.574 --> 00:00:42.017
Your turn. Say: Stall.

13
00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:45.649
Stall.

14
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:47.500
Noodles.

15
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.022
Noodles means long, thin strips of food made from flour or rice.

16
00:00:52.322 --> 00:00:53.997
I love beef noodle soup.

17
00:00:54.697 --> 00:00:57.291
Your turn. Say: Noodles.

18
00:00:59.991 --> 00:01:00.737
Noodles.

19
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:02.403
Grilled.

20
00:01:03.103 --> 00:01:05.079
Grilled means cooked over hot fire.

21
00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:07.750
Grilled corn is my favourite snack.

22
00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:11.068
Your turn. Say: Grilled.

23
00:01:13.768 --> 00:01:14.548
Grilled.

24
00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:16.458
Spicy.

25
00:01:17.158 --> 00:01:19.053
Spicy means hot with chilli.

26
00:01:19.353 --> 00:01:21.179
This sauce is very spicy.

27
00:01:21.879 --> 00:01:24.508
Your turn. Say: Spicy.

28
00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:28.116
Spicy.

29
00:01:29.117 --> 00:01:29.944
Sweet.

30
00:01:30.644 --> 00:01:32.655
Sweet means tasting of sugar.

31
00:01:32.955 --> 00:01:34.827
Num ansom is sweet and sticky.

32
00:01:35.527 --> 00:01:38.643
Your turn. Say: Sweet.

33
00:01:41.343 --> 00:01:42.124
Sweet.

34
00:01:43.117 --> 00:01:43.828
Price.

35
00:01:44.528 --> 00:01:47.038
Price means how much money something costs.

36
00:01:47.338 --> 00:01:49.210
The price is 4,000 riels.

37
00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:52.318
Your turn. Say: Price.

38
00:01:55.018 --> 00:01:55.950
Price.

39
00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:57.661
Clean.

40
00:01:58.361 --> 00:01:59.838
Clean means not dirty.

41
00:02:00.138 --> 00:02:01.731
Choose a clean stall.

42
00:02:02.431 --> 00:02:04.700
Your turn. Say: Clean.

43
00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:07.972
Clean.

44
00:02:08.983 --> 00:02:11.053
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:11.353 --> 00:02:13.758
Sreypich, what's your favourite street food?

46
00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:17.818
Grilled pork with rice. It's delicious!

47
00:02:19.117 --> 00:02:20.385
Is it spicy?

48
00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:24.542
Not really, but the sauce is a bit spicy.

49
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:26.979
And for dessert?

50
00:02:28.283 --> 00:02:32.085
Sweet coconut cakes. And I always choose clean stalls.

51
00:02:33.383 --> 00:02:36.138
Grammar focus: Adjectives for taste.

52
00:02:36.438 --> 00:02:39.766
It's spicy. It's sweet. It's delicious.

53
00:02:40.066 --> 00:02:45.107
Use 'a bit' or 'very' to say how strong a taste is: a bit spicy, very sweet.

54
00:02:46.117 --> 00:02:48.873
Now read and listen. Tastes of the Street.

55
00:02:49.173 --> 00:02:51.417
Cambodia is famous for its street food.

56
00:02:52.717 --> 00:02:56.945
At a stall, you can buy noodles, grilled meat or sweet desserts.

57
00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:02.212
Some food is very spicy, and some is sweet and sticky.

58
00:03:03.517 --> 00:03:06.352
The prices are low, usually just a few thousand riels.

59
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.800
I always choose stalls that are clean.

60
00:03:11.117 --> 00:03:13.444
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:13.744 --> 00:03:15.175
Chilli makes food blank.

62
00:03:15.475 --> 00:03:19.082
A, spicy. B, sweet. C, clean.

63
00:03:23.083 --> 00:03:25.269
The answer is A: spicy.

64
00:03:26.783 --> 00:03:29.526
A small table or shop in the street is a blank.

65
00:03:29.826 --> 00:03:33.061
A, stall. B, price. C, noodle.

66
00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.817
The answer is A: stall.

67
00:03:40.317 --> 00:03:42.316
Cooked over hot fire means blank.

68
00:03:42.616 --> 00:03:46.095
A, grilled. B, sweet. C, spicy.

69
00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:51.653
The answer is A: grilled.

70
00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:56.487
Now it's your turn to speak. What is your favourite street food?

71
00:04:01.787 --> 00:04:07.087
My favourite street food is num pang. It's crunchy and a bit spicy, and the price is cheap.

72
00:04:07.387 --> 00:04:10.153
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:15.137
Great work today! You learned eight new words and adjectives for taste.

74
00:04:15.437 --> 00:04:20.075
Today's value is food safety. Choose clean food and wash your hands.

75
00:04:20.375 --> 00:04:23.027
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

76
00:04:23.327 --> 00:04:26.270
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

